# Domain-Driven Design (DDD) Anti-Patterns

Violations of domain-centric design and rich model principles.

---

## 1. Business Rule Outside Domain

**Context:** When reviewing where business decisions are made. Business logic must live in Domain layer (Entities, Value Objects, Domain Services, UseCases).

**Forbidden:**

```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Business rule in Redux
// src/app/store/vagaSlice.ts
const vagaSlice = createSlice({
  name: 'vaga',
  initialState,
  reducers: {
    publicarVaga: (state, action) => {
      const vaga = state.vagas.find(v => v.id === action.payload);
      
      // Business rule in reducer!
      if (vaga.status !== 'RASCUNHO') {
        throw new Error('Apenas rascunhos podem ser publicados');
      }
      
      // Business calculation
      vaga.dataPublicacao = new Date().toISOString();
      vaga.status = 'PUBLICADA';
    }
  }
});

// ❌ BAD: Business rule in component
// src/presentation/components/vaga/VagaCard.tsx
const podeCandidatar = (vaga: Vaga, usuario: Usuario) => {
  // Business logic in UI!
  if (vaga.status !== 'PUBLICADA') return false;
  if (vaga.dataExpiracao && new Date(vaga.dataExpiracao) < new Date()) return false;
  if (usuario.tipo !== 'CANDIDATO') return false;
  return true;
};

// ❌ BAD: Business rule in API/repository
// src/data/repositories/VagaRepositoryImpl.ts
async function criar(dados: CriarVagaDTO): Promise<Vaga> {
  // Validation in repository!
  if (dados.salarioMinimo > dados.salarioMaximo) {
    throw new Error('Salario minimo nao pode ser maior que maximo');
  }
  
  return this.api.criar(dados);
}
```

**Required:**

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Business rule in Entity
// src/domain/entities/Vaga.ts
export class Vaga {
  private constructor(
    private readonly _id: string,
    private _titulo: string,
    private _status: StatusVaga,
    private _dataPublicacao?: Date,
    private _dataExpiracao?: Date
  ) {}
  
  // Factory method with validation
  static criar(dados: CriarVagaDTO): Resultado<Vaga> {
    if (dados.salarioMinimo > dados.salarioMaximo) {
      return { sucesso: false, erro: 'Salario minimo nao pode ser maior que maximo' };
    }
    
    return {
      sucesso: true,
      dados: new Vaga(
        generateUUID(),
        dados.titulo,
        'RASCUNHO'
      )
    };
  }
  
  // Business behavior encapsulated
  publicar(): Resultado<void> {
    if (this._status !== 'RASCUNHO') {
      return { sucesso: false, erro: 'Apenas rascunhos podem ser publicados' };
    }
    
    this._status = 'PUBLICADA';
    this._dataPublicacao = new Date();
    return { sucesso: true };
  }
  
  // Business query encapsulated
  estaAtiva(): boolean {
    if (this._status !== 'PUBLICADA') return false;
    if (!this._dataExpiracao) return true;
    return this._dataExpiracao > new Date();
  }
  
  podeSerCandidatadaPor(usuario: Usuario): boolean {
    if (!this.estaAtiva()) return false;
    if (usuario.tipo !== 'CANDIDATO') return false;
    return true;
  }
  
  get id(): string { return this._id; }
  get status(): StatusVaga { return this._status; }
  get dataPublicacao(): Date | undefined { return this._dataPublicacao; }
}

// ✅ GOOD: UseCase orchestrates, doesn't contain rules
// src/domain/usecases/vaga/PublicarVagaUseCase.ts
@injectable()
export class PublicarVagaUseCase {
  constructor(
    @inject('VagaRepository') private repo: VagaRepository
  ) {}
  
  async execute(vagaId: string): Promise<Resultado<void>> {
    const vaga = await this.repo.obterPorId(vagaId);
    
    if (!vaga) {
      return { sucesso: false, erro: 'Vaga nao encontrada' };
    }
    
    // Delegate to entity - business rule lives in domain
    const resultado = vaga.publicar();
    
    if (!resultado.sucesso) {
      return resultado;
    }
    
    await this.repo.salvar(vaga);
    return { sucesso: true };
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD: Component uses domain, doesn't implement rules
// src/presentation/components/vaga/VagaCard.tsx
const VagaCard = ({ vaga, usuario }: { vaga: Vaga; usuario: Usuario }) => {
  // Use domain method, don't reimplement logic
  const podeCandidatar = vaga.podeSerCandidatadaPor(usuario);
  
  return (
    <Card>
      <StatusBadge status={vaga.status} />
      {podeCandidatar && <CandidatarButton />}
    </Card>
  );
};
```

**Where Business Rules Belong:**

| Type | Location | Example |
|------|----------|---------|
| Entity lifecycle | Entity static factory | `Vaga.criar()` with validation |
| State transitions | Entity methods | `vaga.publicar()`, `vaga.cancelar()` |
| Calculations | Entity methods or Value Objects | `vaga.calcularSalarioTotal()` |
| Cross-entity rules | Domain Services | `RecomendacaoService.calcularMatch()` |
| Orchestration | UseCases | `PublicarVagaUseCase` calls repo + notifications |
| Invariants | Entity validation | `vaga.validar()` enforces rules |

**Impact:**

- Procedural system - domain is just data bags
- Weak domain model - can't trust objects to be valid
- Scattered rules - hard to find where decisions are made
- Duplication - same validation in multiple places
- Testing difficulty - need UI to test business logic

**Detection:**

- `if/else` logic in components beyond UI state
- Validation in API calls
- State change conditions in Redux reducers
- Calculations in `.tsx` files
- Complex `disabled={...}` logic in JSX

**Architecture Reference:**

See `@ARCHITECTURE.md` Section 5: "Regra de negocio em Entities ou UseCases. Nao em Redux, Components, API ou Repository."

