## 3. Entities as DTOs

**Context:** When designing entities. Entities should encapsulate behavior, not just be data structures.

**Forbidden:**

```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Entity as DTO (data bag)
// src/domain/entities/Feedback.ts
export interface Feedback {
  id: string;
  comentario: string;
  nivel: number;
  dataCriacao: string;
  // No methods, no encapsulation
}

// ❌ BAD: Even worse - plain object
// src/domain/entities/Vaga.ts
export type Vaga = {
  id: string;
  titulo: string;
  status: string;
  // No behavior at all
};
```

**Required:**

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Rich Entity with behavior
// src/domain/entities/Feedback.ts
export class Feedback {
  private constructor(
    private readonly _id: string,
    private _comentario: string,
    private _nivel: number,
    private _dataCriacao: Date,
    private _status: StatusFeedback = 'ATIVO'
  ) {}
  
  // Factory method with validation
  static criar(dados: CriarFeedbackDTO): Resultado<Feedback> {
    // Validation in factory
    if (dados.nivel < 1 || dados.nivel > 5) {
      return { sucesso: false, erro: 'Nivel deve estar entre 1 e 5' };
    }
    
    if ((dados.nivel === 1 || dados.nivel === 2) && !dados.comentario?.trim()) {
      return { sucesso: false, erro: 'Comentario obrigatorio para niveis baixos' };
    }
    
    return {
      sucesso: true,
      dados: new Feedback(
        generateUUID(),
        dados.comentario,
        dados.nivel,
        new Date()
      )
    };
  }
  
  // Business behavior
  editarComentario(novoComentario: string): Resultado<void> {
    if (this._status !== 'ATIVO') {
      return { sucesso: false, erro: 'Nao e possivel editar feedback inativo' };
    }
    
    this._comentario = novoComentario;
    return { sucesso: true };
  }
  
  inativar(): void {
    this._status = 'INATIVO';
  }
  
  // Business queries
  estaAtivo(): boolean {
    return this._status === 'ATIVO';
  }
  
  requerComentario(): boolean {
    return this._nivel === 1 || this._nivel === 2;
  }
  
  getLabelNivel(): string {
    const labels = {
      1: 'Precisa evoluir bastante',
      2: 'Abaixo do esperado',
      3: 'Dentro do esperado',
      4: 'Acima do esperado',
      5: 'Referencia para os demais'
    };
    return labels[this._nivel];
  }
  
  // Getters for read access
  get id(): string { return this._id; }
  get comentario(): string { return this._comentario; }
  get nivel(): number { return this._nivel; }
  get dataCriacao(): Date { return this._dataCriacao; }
  get status(): StatusFeedback { return this._status; }
}

// ✅ GOOD: Value Object for complex types
// src/domain/value-objects/Periodo.ts
export class Periodo {
  private constructor(
    private readonly _inicio: Date,
    private readonly _fim: Date
  ) {}
  
  static criar(inicio: Date, fim: Date): Resultado<Periodo> {
    if (inicio >= fim) {
      return { sucesso: false, erro: 'Data inicio deve ser anterior a data fim' };
    }
    return { sucesso: true, dados: new Periodo(inicio, fim) };
  }
  
  contem(data: Date): boolean {
    return data >= this._inicio && data <= this._fim;
  }
  
  dias(): number {
    const diff = this._fim.getTime() - this._inicio.getTime();
    return Math.ceil(diff / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));
  }
  
  get inicio(): Date { return this._inicio; }
  get fim(): Date { return this._fim; }
}
```

**Entity vs DTO:**

| Characteristic | Entity (Domain) | DTO (Data Transfer) |
|----------------|-----------------|---------------------|
| Has behavior | Yes (methods) | No (data only) |
| Encapsulation | Private fields, public methods | Public fields |
| Validation | In constructor/factory | External |
| Identity | Has ID, tracked | Just data |
| Mutability | Controlled via methods | Often mutable |
| Location | `domain/entities/` | `shared/types/` or `data/dtos/` |

**Impact:**

- Loss of encapsulation - anyone can modify entity state
- Scattered rules - validation happens in many places
- Invalid states - entities can exist in impossible states
- Testing difficulty - can't trust entity is valid

**Detection:**

- `interface` instead of `class` for entities
- Entities with no methods (only getters/setters)
- Direct property assignment to entities
- Validation happening outside entity
- `type` alias for entities

**Refactoring Strategy:**

| From | To |
|------|-----|
| Interface with properties | Class with private fields |
| External validation | Factory method with validation |
| Direct property access | Getter methods |
| External state changes | Entity methods (e.g., `ativar()`, `cancelar()`) |
| Scattered calculations | Entity methods or Value Objects |

