## 4. Feature Coupled to Backend

**Context:** When frontend assumes backend behavior or replicates backend rules.

**Forbidden:**

```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Frontend reproduces backend rule
// src/domain/usecases/vaga/CalcularSalarioUseCase.ts
@injectable()
export class CalcularSalarioUseCase {
  execute(valor: number, tipo: TipoContrato): number {
    // Frontend guessing backend calculation!
    if (tipo === 'CLT') {
      return valor * 1.3; // Assuming 30% benefits
    }
    return valor;
  }
}

// ❌ BAD: Frontend assumes backend behavior
// src/presentation/components/candidatura/CandidaturaCard.tsx
const podeCancelar = (candidatura: Candidatura) => {
  // Frontend assuming backend rule!
  const diffHours = (Date.now() - candidatura.dataCriacao.getTime()) / (1000 * 60 * 60);
  return diffHours < 24 && candidatura.status === 'PENDENTE';
};
```

**Required:**

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Frontend asks backend for calculations
// src/domain/usecases/vaga/ObterSalarioCalculadoUseCase.ts
@injectable()
export class ObterSalarioCalculadoUseCase {
  constructor(
    @inject('CalculadoraApi') private api: CalculadoraApi
  ) {}
  
  async execute(valor: number, tipo: TipoContrato): Promise<number> {
    // Backend owns the calculation
    const response = await this.api.calcular({ valor, tipo });
    return response.retorno;
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD: Frontend delegates to backend
// src/presentation/components/candidatura/CandidaturaCard.tsx
const CandidaturaCard = ({ candidatura }: { candidatura: Candidatura }) => {
  const container = useContainer();
  const verificarUseCase = container.resolve(VerificarCancelamentoUseCase);
  const [podeCancelar, setPodeCancelar] = useState(false);
  
  useEffect(() => {
    // Ask backend if can cancel
    verificarUseCase.execute(candidatura.id)
      .then(resultado => setPodeCancelar(resultado.podeCancelar));
  }, [candidatura.id]);
};

// ✅ GOOD: Backend endpoint for business rule
// src/domain/usecases/candidatura/VerificarCancelamentoUseCase.ts
@injectable()
export class VerificarCancelamentoUseCase {
  constructor(
    @inject('CandidaturaRepository') private repo: CandidaturaRepository
  ) {}
  
  async execute(candidaturaId: string): Promise<VerificacaoResult> {
    const candidatura = await this.repo.obterPorId(candidaturaId);
    if (!candidatura) {
      return { podeCancelar: false, motivo: 'Candidatura nao encontrada' };
    }
    
    // Backend decides, frontend just shows result
    return {
      podeCancelar: candidatura.podeSerCancelada(),
      motivo: candidatura.podeSerCancelada() ? null : 'Prazo de cancelamento expirado'
    };
  }
}
```

**Principle:**

- Frontend: Handles UI, user interactions, display logic
- Backend: Owns business rules, calculations, validations, state transitions
- API Contract: Backend exposes what frontend can/can't do

**Impact:**

- Logic duplication - same rule in two places
- Future divergence - backend changes, frontend doesn't know
- Stale assumptions - frontend logic becomes outdated
- Security issues - client-side validation can be bypassed

**Detection:**

- Calculations in domain that match backend logic
- Client-side validation without server validation
- Assumptions about state transitions
- Time-based logic in frontend ("within 24 hours")
- Status transitions checked in frontend

**Architecture Reference:**

See `@ARCHITECTURE.md` Section 5: "Frontend nao deve reproduzir regra do backend nem assumir comportamento implicito."

